  "body": "#905: outside Area mode, law (b) read an arc move only at its chord joints. A sharp wall or island corner between two joints was never measured against the cutter. The issue's case: a 4 mm cutter on an r 200 arc sweeping 0.048 rad, with the corner midway between joints, passed a 90 um gouge on main (after #839's union of both joint sets).\r\n\r\nFork synced at v0.17.0, PROCESS_VERSION 14; merged with upstream main at bac4d015 (head 8207e79e).\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- **New `sim::verify::arc_wall`** (`crates/sim/src/verify/arc_wall.rs`): the XY trace of a move (`Trace::Seg`, `Trace::Arc`, `Trace::Unread`) and the exact least distance from a wall edge to an arc.\r\n  - For each piece of the edge inside the arc's wedge, the distance is radial. `|CP|` is convex along a segment, so it is the gap between that piece's radius range and the circle.\r\n  - Outside the wedge, the nearest arc point is an endpoint.\r\n  - The radius is a band, `[min, max]` of the two endpoint radii, widened by `ARC_PAD` (1 um, the centre lattice). The reading is never farther than the truth.\r\n- **`section::tangency`**: in `Mode::Boundary` an XY arc (a helix included) now joins the whole-move wall reading (`wall_gouge`) that straight moves have had since #43. Edge classification is unchanged:\r\n  - section edges are walls;\r\n  - with a model, the probe picks the walls;\r\n  - without one, a move that properly crosses a region edge is over an open rim. For an arc, the crossing is computed on the true circle.\r\n\r\n  A straight move keeps the same squared comparison, float for float.\r\n- **Unchanged:** Area mode, which already reads every chord whole. XZ/YZ arcs, whose XY trace is not a circle, keep the joint reading. The #689 joint union also stays, since it still judges the section's containment and the non-wall edges.\r\n- A centre or radius that is not a number fails closed (a gouge). A zero-radius or zero-sweep arc is read as its straight chord, as `cl::arc_chords` cuts it.\r\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/905-arc-corner-gouge.md`.\r\n\r\n## How it was tested\r\n\r\nNew pinning tests:\r\n- `crates/app/tests/boundary_arc_walls.rs`, the issue's Done-means. Each case runs the arc ccw and cw, with the vertex outside and inside the circle.\r\n  - `a_corner_between_an_arcs_joints_past_the_floor_is_a_gouge`: the corner sits midway between the joints at 3.5, 3.8, 3.90 and 3.98 mm (floor 3.99). The test asserts that the joints of both tolerances read the 3.90 corner clear, so the old reading passed it. Every case is now a gouge.\r\n  - `the_same_corner_just_inside_the_floor_stays_clean`: 3.995, 4.0 and 4.5 mm pass.\r\n  - `area_mode_verdicts_on_the_corner_are_unchanged`.\r\n- `sim::verify::arc_wall::tests::the_exact_distance_matches_a_dense_sampling`: 800 random segments against four arcs (ccw and cw, under and over a half turn). The exact distance is never farther than a dense sampling and stays within its spacing.\r\n\r\nChecked against the old code: with the arc kept out of the wall reading, `a_corner_between_an_arcs_joints_past_the_floor_is_a_gouge` fails at the 3.90 mm case. With the fix, it passes.\r\n\r\nGates:\r\n- On the final head 8207e79e (after merging upstream main at bac4d015):\r\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green.\r\n  - The Boundary-mode suites listed below: green.\r\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n  - `headless_bin`: green now that #936 is fixed upstream.\r\n\r\nEarlier runs, on the tree before that merge:\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (before the clippy respelling): green (sim, motion and app suites, `verify_arc_reading` among them).\r\n- The quick gate's maps don't name the Boundary-mode suites, so these were also run by hand, all green:\r\n  - `boundary_walls`, `wall_arc_entry`, `corner_blend`, `verify`\r\n  - `blind_floor`, `real_tip_contour`, `solid_law`, `solid_law_goldens`, `vertical_arc_entry`\r\n- `cargo xtask gate batch` (24.8 min): this PR's suites are green, but the batch was not green overall. Results by step:\r\n  - geometry, tools, post, sim, motion (slow ones included) and app (center_cut_multiaxis included): green.\r\n  - clippy failed on two `!(x >= y)` NaN guards in `arc_wall.rs`. They were respelled (3ad9b07f), and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is now clean.\r\n  - The first ui run failed to compile on a stale build cache (`ash` rlib missing); a rerun built. Of 17 ui test binaries, 16 pass. The one failure is `theme_files::the_shipped_example_parses` (cell_h 35 -> 40), red on upstream main already (#932). This PR touches no ui code.\r\n  - cl: `headless_bin::cl_bin_prints_move_stats` fails. Upstream main is red there too (#936: #839's golden regeneration made `contour_disc_hole.cl` 33 arcs, the test still expects 30). This PR touches no cl code or golden.\r\n- No snapshot PNG touched.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- A model-backed Boundary case (a section edge, or a region edge classified as a wall by the probe) has no new test of its own. That classification code is unchanged, and the model-backed suites above pass.\r\n- XZ/YZ arcs are not read on their true trace (unchanged, see above).\r\n\r\nChangelog: Gouge check: in Boundary mode (contour, trace, face) an arc move is checked along its whole length against wall corners, not only at sample points, so a gouge between two samples is caught (#905)\r\n\r\nEffort: high (the issue's label). Not escalated.\r\n\r\nFixes #905\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
